  "id": "melanocyte-stimulating-hormone",
  "term": "melanocyte-stimulating hormone",
  "definition": "Melanocyte-stimulating hormone is a group of peptide hormones that increase pigmentation by stimulating melanocytes and related pigment cells to make and distribute melanin. These hormones are derived from pro-opiomelanocortin and are produced in parts of the pituitary and hypothalamus.",
